    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "McGuirk Beggan Property is delighted to introduce No. 38 St. Teresa`s Road, a charming 1950s-built three-bedroom semi-detached family home overlooking the much-loved Stannaway Park.\n\nWhile the property is now in need of modernisation, it retains many of the features that give homes of this era their enduring appeal, including handsome bay windows to the front, generous ceiling heights, original fireplaces and a wonderful sense of space throughout. For those with vision, this is a house with tremendous potential a chance to take a solid, well-proportioned home and breathe new life into it, while creating something that feels entirely your own.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises an entrance porch, welcoming entrance hall, guest WC, living room, dining room and kitchen at ground floor level, with three bedrooms, a separate WC and bathroom upstairs. There is also the added benefit of a substantial garage, offering exciting possibilities for future conversion and extension, subject of course to the necessary planning permission.\n\nOutside, the property continues to impress. To the front there is generous off-street parking for two cars, while the rear garden is a particular highlight. Enjoying a coveted westerly aspect, it is a wonderfully private space with plenty of room to create a beautiful garden for relaxing, entertaining and family life. Access to the garden is also available through the garage.\n\nSt. Teresa`s Road is a particularly special residential setting, and homes here rarely come to the market. This exceptionally peaceful, tree-lined avenue has an established community feel and is perfectly positioned for those who want the tranquillity of a mature residential neighbourhood while remaining within easy reach of the city.\n\nCrumlin Village and Ashleaf Shopping Centre are just a short stroll away, providing a wealth of everyday amenities, while the city centre is approximately two miles away. There is also an excellent choice of schools, parks, transport links and recreational facilities close by.\n\nThere is something wonderfully appealing about a house that has been part of a neighbourhood for generations, retaining the proportions and character of its era while offering the next owner the opportunity to write its next chapter.\n\nNo. 38 is a home with good bones, wonderful outdoor space and enormous potential. For the discerning buyer willing to roll up their sleeves, this could be a very rewarding project a chance to transform a much-loved 1950s home into something truly special, in an exceptionally sought-after location.\n\nSolid from the gate to the end of the rear garden a rare opportunity, with untold possibilities and a wealth of potential awaiting its next owner."
      },
